# Offline twin note — pw-uks-fe-smearing

Atomiverse pin: collinear UKS plane-wave NC-UPF BCC Fe with Fermi–Dirac
metallic smearing (`regressions/pw/pw-uks-fe-smearing/REFERENCE.md`).

Absolute energy is **not** compared to CP2K (GTH-GPW ≠ NC-UPF PW) — same
class of limitation as `pw-smearing-al` and `pw-uks-kmesh-fe`.

Algorithm twin (documentation only), if re-running CP2K offline:

- `&FORCE_EVAL` METHOD Quickstep, UKS / LSD
- Fe GTH (e.g. GTH-PBE-q16 or available Fe PP in the module data dir)
- `&SMEAR METHOD FERMI_DIRAC` with electronic temperature matching
  `degauss ≈ 0.02` Ry (≈ 3158 K)
- Monkhorst–Pack k-mesh matching the ATV pin when fair
- Optional input skeleton: `fe_uks_smear.inp` (add when a CP2K binary is
  available on the pin host)

No live CP2K at ctest.
